-- Rows 0 and 1 despawn, so the world shrinks to 4 rows while old row 2 still stores mentor 5 — at or beyond the new row count. A positional gather is a hard BQN index fault; the algebra owes a mask clear or a correct read, never a fault path. Resolving by index-of against the filtered fixture-row column finds old row 5 (dead) at its new slot 3, and old row 2 loses Trained.
-- Expect over survivors (old rows 2 3 4 5): only old row 2 hops onto a dead master; old row 4's mentor (old row 2) is alive, the dangling rows never pass.
--! registry ../registries/027-hop-out-of-range.reg
--! expect-n 4
--! expect trained = 0 1 1 1

Cursed , ~
Nord & mentor.Dead , -Trained
